  "finding": "TYPED_SERIALIZED_BAG predicts one class on all 128 protected cases, and that class is exactly half the split, so 0.5 is a prior and not a measurement. 32 of 128 cases lie within 0.05 of the boundary and the runner-up is correct on all 32, so tipping that set gives 0.5 + 32/128 = 0.75 exactly. The archived and replayed values are two sides of one boundary on an unresponsive comparator, not two measurements that disagree.",
